 ## Background
-Hard Sample Mining was introduced by J. Korhonen et al. in the paper "Efficient NeRF Optimization -- Not All Samples Remain Equally Hard" [S1]. The method was applied to PyTorch reimplementations of Instant-NGP and Nerfacto on Mip-NeRF-360 and NeRF synthetic datasets [S1]. It is distinct from Nerfacc's approach of pruning low-weight samples, as HSM uses propagated pixel loss to rank and subsample [S1].
+Hard Sample Mining was introduced by J. Korhonen et al. in the paper "Efficient NeRF Optimization -- Not All Samples Remain Equally Hard" (2024) [S1]. It was applied to PyTorch reimplementations of Instant-NGP and Nerfacto on Mip-NeRF-360 and synthetic NeRF datasets [S1]. The method differs from Nerfacc's pruning approach by using propagated pixel loss to rank and subsample a hard minibatch [S1].
 
